## Find your way

[% if workflows %]
- [Project context](.context/README.md) explains the installed workflows.
[% endif %]
[% for language in languages %]
- [The [[ language | capitalize ]] workspace](src/[[ language ]]/README.md) explains code and commands.
[% endfor %]
[% if agents %]
- [AgentSync](.agents/README.md) manages shared instructions and native configuration.
[% endif %]
- [Architecture](ARCHITECTURE.md) explains ownership and updates.

Edit source[% if workflows %], run `just sync`[% endif %], then `just check`.
Formatting and synchronization are explicit writes. External links run separately
through `just links`.
[% if secrets %]

SecretSpec resolves credentials only for `just secret-run COMMAND`.
Configure a provider and declarations when needed; shell entry never loads secrets.
[% endif %]

## Update

Commit local work, then run:

```bash
env -u PYTHONPATH -u PYTHONHOME uvx --from copier==9.16.0 copier update
```

Review the diff and conflicts, run setup[% if workflows %], sync[% endif %]
and check. Copier selects the latest stable tag from the source saved in
`.copier-answers.yml`; add `--vcs-ref TAG` to choose a specific release.
Adding capabilities preserves saved selections. Removing them
requires manual migration because Copier can remove previously owned paths.
Actual records remain project-owned.

This project started with [Exordio](https://github.com/marcusinthesky/exordio).
